nt; only their file paths changed.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nNo further external dependencies added; DEP remains deterministic.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-28T00:41:51.209Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###phase1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: PHASE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"All three Director-level DEPs (Frontend/UI, Authentication/Security, and Content-Management/Admin) have been delivered, cross-checked, and reconciled to the same Next.js App-Router architecture.  They are each deterministic, file-level clear, and mutually consistent.  No further open questions remain.  We can therefore compile them into a single, step-ordered Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) for the entire HOA website and proceed to the Execution phase.\\\",\\n  \\\"depString\\\": \\\"────────────────────────────────────────\\\\nHOA WEBSITE – MASTER DETERMINISTICALLY EXECUTABLE PLAN (DEP)\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\nThis document merges the three domain DEPs (Frontend v2, Auth v1, Admin v1) into one execution roadmap.  File paths are relative to repository root.\\\\n\\\\n0. PREREQUISITES\\\\n   • Node 18+  • npm 9+  • Git  • Vercel CLI  • Firebase CLI  • jq (for scripts)\\\\n   • Two Firebase projects already reserved: hoa-portal-dev, hoa-portal-prod.\\\\n   • Vercel account with GitHub linkage.\\\\n\\\\n1. INITIAL REPOSITORY & TOOLING\\\\n   1.1  npx create-next-app@latest hoa-portal --typescript --tailwind --eslint --app --no-src-dir --import-alias \\\\\\\"@/*\\\\\\\"\\\\n   1.2  cd hoa-portal && git init && git remote add origin <repo-url>\\\\n   1.3  npm i firebase @firebase/auth @firebase/firestore @firebase/storage\\\\n   1.4  npm i @tiptap/react @tiptap/starter-kit @tiptap/extension-markdown marked react-use clsx\\\\n   1.5  npm i -D jest @testing-library/react axe-playwright @playwright/test\\\\n\\\\n2. GLOBAL STRUCTURE (App Router)\\\\n   app/\\