uthContext.tsx\\\\\\\\n  ThemeContext.tsx\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nhooks/\\\\\\\\n  useAuth.ts                        // wraps context, JWT helpers\\\\\\\\n  useBreakpoint.ts                  // responsive helpers\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nlib/\\\\\\\\n  auth.ts                           // token handling, guard helpers\\\\\\\\n  api.ts                            // axios / fetch wrapper\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nstyles/\\\\\\\\n  globals.css (imports Tailwind base, custom CSS)\\\\\\\\n  tailwind.config.js\\\\\\\\n  theme.ts (color palette for non-TW solutions if needed)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\npublic/\\\\\\\\n  logo.svg, docs/, etc.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n3. Navigation & Responsiveness\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nHeader\\\\\\\\n • Logo (left) → Home\\\\\\\\n • Primary links: Home, Bylaws, Schools, Contact\\\\\\\\n • Auth-aware links:\\\\\\\\n   • If not signed in: “Login”\\\\\\\\n   • If signed in: “Dues, Meetings, News & Events” + avatar menu (profile/logout)\\\\\\\\n • Mobile ≤ 768 px: Hamburger opens MobileMenu (animated slide-in)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nFooter\\\\\\\\n • Copyright, HOA address, quick links, social icons\\\\\\\\n • Stack → single column ≤ 640 px; 3-column grid ≥ 768 px\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nBreakpoints (Tailwind default)\\\\\\\\n • sm 640px | md 768px | lg 1024px | xl 1280px | 2xl 1536px\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n4. Visual Style System\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nChoice: Tailwind CSS + custom config (fast, utility-first, A11y-friendly).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nColors (placed in tailwind.config.js → theme.extend.colors)\\\\\\\\n • primary: #004880 (brand blue)\\\\\\\\n • secondary: #00AEEF (accent)\\\\\\\\n • neutral-100/900: grayscale\\\\\\\\n • success / warning / error semantic colors\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nTypography\\\\\\\\n • Font-family: ‘Inter’, sans-serif (fallback system UI)\\\\\\\\n • Base font-size: 16 px; scale via Tailwind text-sm/md/lg/…\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nSpacing\\\\\\\\n • 4-pt scale via Tailwind (p-1 == 4 px, etc.)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nShadow / Radius\\\\\\\\n • Customize via tailwind.config → boxShadow / borderRadius\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nGlobal styles in globals.css: reset, focus-ring helpers.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n5. Accessibility (WCAG 2.1 AA)\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n• Semantic HTML5 elements (header/nav/main/footer/section/article).\\\\\\\\n• Ensure color-contrast ≥ 4.5:1; verify with automated tests.\\\\\\\\n• Keyboard-navigable menus & modals; visible focus outline.\\\\\\\\n• ARIA attributes for mobile menu (`aria-expanded`, `aria-controls`).\\\\\\\\n• `lang=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"en\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"` root attribute; meta viewport for zoom.\\\\\\\\n• Form inputs with associated `<label>`; error messages with `aria-live`.\\\\\\\\n• Skip-to-content link.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n6. Shared Context / Providers\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nAuthProvider (context/AuthContext.tsx)\\\\\\\\n • Stores JWT & user role; exposes `login`, `logout`, `user`, `isAdmin`.\\\\\\\\n • Provided in _app.tsx.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThemeProvider (context/ThemeContext.tsx) – lightweight; toggles light/dark if desired.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nProtectedRoute / AdminRoute wrappers (components/layout)\\\\\\\\n • Client-side guard (redirect to /login).\\\\\\\\n • For SSR, pages export `getServerSideProps` using lib/auth.ts to verify cookie.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n7. Delegation Map for Execution Phase (OFAAT principle)\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nSupervisor-level work packages:\\\\\\\\n S-1 Layout & Navigation\\\\\\\\n   • components/layout/* (Header, Footer, MobileMenu, wrappers)\\\\\\\\n   • _app.tsx integration of providers\\\\\\\\n S-2 Public Pages\\\\\\\\n   • pages/index.tsx, contact.tsx, bylaws.tsx, schools.tsx, 404.tsx\\\\\\\\n S-3 Auth & Member Pages\\\\\\\\n   • login.tsx + forms/LoginForm.tsx\\\\\\\\n   • dues/, meetings/, news-events/ pages & dynamic routes\\\\\\\\n S-4 Admin Dashboard\\\\\\\\n   • pages/admin/dashboard.tsx + required UI components\\\\\\\\n S-5 Styling & Theming\\\\\\\\n   • Tailwind integration, globals.css, tailwind.config.js, theme.ts\\\\\\\\n S-6 Accessibility & Testing\\\\\\\\n   • Implement axe-core CI check, unit tests for nav focus, contrast audit script\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nEach supervisor will recruit attendant agents per file (OFAAT) and ensure ESLint/Prettier pass.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nDependencies / External Assumptions (minimal)\\\\\\\\n• Tailwind CSS and PostCSS setup (deterministic via `npx tailwindcss init -p`).\\\\\\\\n• Auth API endpoints assumed existing (/api/login, /api/me); stubs can be mocked.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis DEP is deterministic, file-level clear, and ready for Execution once approved.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"ord_a1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order plan-auth-v1 from agent 3: DEP – Authentication & Security for HOA Portal  (Revision: v1, author: Seratt, rank: Director)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n0.  PURPOSE & SCOPE\\\\\\\\nDesign a deterministic, file-level plan (DEP) covering Firebase project creation, authentication flows, role/claim management, Firestore security rules, protected-route strategy in Next.js 13+, required environment variables, and an explicit delegate-ready task breakdown for the Execution phase.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1.  KEY ASSUMPTIONS\\\\\\\\n• HOA website is built on Next.js 13 (app router) with TypeScript.\\\\\\\\n• Firebase will be the sole backend (Auth, Firestore, Storage, Cloud Functions).\\\\\\\\n• We maintain two Firebase projects: dev and prod.\\\\\\\\n• CI/CD via Vercel; Firebase CLI available in build images.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2.  DETERMINISTIC NAMING CONVENTIONS\\\\\\\\n| Context | Name Pattern | Example (prod) | Example (dev) |\\\\\\\\n|---------|--------------|----------------|----------------|\\\\\\\\n| Firebase projectId | <org>-portal-<env> | hoa-portal-prod | hoa-portal-dev |\\\\\\\\n| Firebase storage bucket | <projectId>.appspot.com | hoa-portal-prod.appspot.com | … |\\\\\\\\n| Firestore collection IDs | kebab-case plural | dues-docs, meeting-minutes, news, bylaws |\\\\\\\\n| Auth custom claim keys | camelCase | role |\\\\\\\\n| Cloud Function region | us-central1 | — | — |\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3.  STEP-BY-STEP EXECUTABLE PLAN\\\\\\\\nA. Firebase Project Setup (repeat for dev & prod)\\\\\\\\n   A1. Login & create projects:\\\\\\\\n       firebase login --no-localhost\\\\\\\\n       firebase projects:create hoa-portal-<env> --display-name \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"HOA Portal (<ENV>)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   A2. Enable products:\\\\\\\\n       firebase services:set firestore.googleapis.com\\\\\\\\n       firebase services:set identitytoolkit.googleapis.com   # Auth\\\\\\\\n       firebase services:set storage-component.googleapis.com # Storage\\\\\\\\n   A3. Initialize local workspace (run once):\\\\\\\\n       firebase init hosting firestore storage functions --project hoa-portal-dev\\\\\\\\n   A4. Set default Firestore location: us-central.\\\\\\\\n   A5. Create CI service account (\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"vercel-deploy-sa\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") and download key JSON (store in Vercel secret).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nB. Auth Configuration\\\\\\\\n   B1. Enable Email/Password sign-in:  gcloud identity toolkit configs update --project hoa-portal-<env> --sign-in-method EMAIL_PASSWORD\\\\\\\\n   B2. Toggle Social Providers through Remote Config param socialAuthEnabled (bool, default false).  Front-end reads param to conditionally render provider buttons.\\\\\\\\n   B3. Configure Password Reset email template (custom HOA branding).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nC. Role & Custom Claims Model\\\\\\\\n   • role ∈ {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"resident\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"boardMember\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"admin\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\n   • Cloud Function (setCustomClaims) restricted to admin account(s):\\\\\\\\n       functions/auth/onCreate.ts → Assign default \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"resident\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".\\\\\\\\n       functions/https/setRole.ts  → Callable; validates requester is admin.\\\\\\\\n   • Claims cached in client; refresh logic on token change.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nD. Firestore Data Model\\\\\\\\n   dues-docs (collection)\\\\\\\\n     └─ <docId> { title, url, amount, dueDate }\\\\\\\\n   meeting-minutes\\\\\\\\n     └─ <docId> { title, url, meetingDate }\\\\\\\\n   news\\\\\\\\n     └─ <docId> { title, body, createdAt }\\\\\\\\n   bylaws (singleton doc bylaws/current { url, version })\\\\\\\\n   users (UID doc) { displayName, email, role (mirror of custom claim) }\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nE. Firestore Security Rules  (firestore.rules)\\\\\\\\n   rules_version = '2';\\\\\\\\n   service cloud.firestore {\\\\\\\\n     match /databases/{db}/documents {\\\\\\\\n       // Public read-only collection\\\\\\\\n       match /bylaws/{docId} {\\\\\\\\n         allow read: if true;\\\\\\\\n         allow write: if isBoardMember();\\\\\\\\n       }\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n       // Auth-required, role-guarded collections\\\\\\\\n       match /dues-docs/{docId} {\\\\\\\\n         allow read:  if isResident();\\\\\\\\n         allow write: if isBoardMember();\\\\\\\\n       }\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n       match /meeting-minutes/{docId} {\\\\\\\\n         allow read:  if isResident();\\\\\\\\n         allow write: if isBoardMember();\\\\\\\\n       }\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n       match /news/{docId} {\\\\\\\\n         allow read:  if isResident();\\\\\\\\n         allow write: if isBoardMember();\\\\\\\\n       }\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n       match /users/{userId} {\\\\\\\\n         allow read, write: if request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == userId;\\\\\\\\n       }\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n       function isResident()     { return request.auth != null; }\\\\\\\\n       function isBoardMember()  { return request.auth.token.role == 'boardMember' || isAdmin(); }\\\\\\\\n       function isAdmin()        { return request.auth.token.role == 'admin'; }\\\\\\\\n     }\\\\\\\\n   }\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nF. Storage Rules (storage.rules)\\\\\\\\n   service firebase.storage {\\\\\\\\n     match /b/{bucket}/o {\\\\\\\\n       match /uploads/{allPaths=**} {\\\\\\\\n         allow read:  if request.auth != null;\\\\\\\\n         allow write: if request.auth.token.role in ['boardMember','admin'];\\\\\\\\n       }\\\\\\\\n     }\\\\\\\\n   }\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nG. Next.js Protected Route Strategy\\\\\\\\n   • Implement app/middleware.ts (Edge Runtime). Logic:\\\\\\\\n       1. Extract Firebase session token cookie.\\\\\\\\n       2. Verify via Admin SDK (cached JWKS) → decode claims.\\\\\\\\n       3. For matched \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"protected\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" routes (/dashboard/**, /minutes/**, /dues/**):\\\\\\\\n          – If no token → redirect to /login.\\\\\\\\n          – If token && missing boardMember role and path starts with /admin → 403.\\\\\\\\n   • Provide useAuth() context hook (client) to expose user & role.\\\\\\\\n   • HOC fallback for CSR pages (older routes) located at src/components/withAuth.tsx.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nH. Environment Variables\\\\\\\\n   # Shared (dev & prod) ─────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n   NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=<firebaseConfig.apiKey>\\\\\\\\n   NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=<projectId>.firebaseapp.com\\\\\\\\n   NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=<projectId>\\\\\\\\n   NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=<projectId>.appspot.com\\\\\\\\n   NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=<id>\\\\\\\\n   NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=<id>\\\\\\\\n   NEXT_PUBLIC_REMOTE_CONFIG_DEFAULTS='{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"socialAuthEnabled\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":false}'\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n   # Server-side only (set in Vercel encrypted vars)\\\\\\\\n   FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY_JSON=@@base64(service-account.json)@@\\\\\\\\n   COOKIE_SECRET_SIGNING=<32+char-random>\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nI.  EXECUTION-PHASE TASK & FILE MATRIX (OFAAT-ready)\\\\\\\\n| File / Artifact                                | Owner (Supervisor) | Notes |\\\\\\\\n|-----------------------------------------------|--------------------|-------|\\\\\\\\n| firebase.json & .firebaserc                   | Supervisor-Infra   | projectId aliases, hosting config |\\\\\\\\n| firestore.rules (section E template)          | Supervisor-Infra   | includes functions isResident()… |\\\\\\\\n| storage.rules (section F)                     | Supervisor-Infra   | — |\\\\\\\\n| functions/auth/onCreate.ts                    | Supervisor-Functions | default role assignment |\\\\\\\\n| functions/https/setRole.ts                    | Supervisor-Functions | callable secured by admin claim |\\\\\\\\n| src/lib/firebaseClient.ts                     | Supervisor-FE Auth | initialize client SDK w/ envs |\\\\\\\\n| src/lib/firebaseAdmin.ts                      | Supervisor-FE Auth | admin SDK w/ credential cache |\\\\\\\\n| src/context/AuthContext.tsx                   | Supervisor-FE Auth | useAuth hook provider |\\\\\\\\n| src/components/withAuth.tsx                   | Supervisor-FE Auth | CSR guard HOC |\\\\\\\\n| app/middleware.ts                              | Supervisor-FE Auth | edge-runtime guard |\\\\\\\\n| scripts/set-remote-config.ts                  | Supervisor-Infra   | CI script to toggle socialAuthEnabled |\\\\\\\\n| docs/DEP-auth-v1.md                           | Supervisor-PMO     | copy of this document in repo |\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4.  COMPLETION CRITERIA\\\\\\\\n• Firebase projects created with exact IDs.\\\\\\\\n• Auth & Social toggle operational; claims issued.\\\\\\\\n• Rules deployed & enforced; verified by security-rules:dryrun.\\\\\\\\n• Next.js guarded routes redirect or 403 correctly.\\\\\\\\n• All env vars supplied in Vercel dashboard and .env.local.sample.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nEND OF DEP\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"ord_ad1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order plan-admin-v1 from agent 2: Content Management & Admin Dashboard – Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP)\\\\\\\\nOrder Sequence ID: plan-admin-v1\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n0. Scope & Assumptions\\\\\\\\n• Project already uses Next.js 14 (App Router) + TypeScript.\\\\\\\\n• Firebase project exists with Firestore, Storage, and Authentication enabled.\\\\\\\\n• Repository root = “/”. All paths below are relative to repo root.\\\\\\\\n• CI/CD (e.g., Vercel) redeploys on main-branch push; preview deploys on PRs.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n1. Information Architecture (admin side)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n Route (app/)                  Purpose\\\\\\\\n ────────────────────────────  ────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n /admin                        Dashboard index\\\\\\\\n /admin/news                   List + “Add News”\\\\\\\\n /admin/news/new               Create News item\\\\\\\\n /admin/news/[id]              Edit News item\\\\\\\\n /admin/minutes                Upload + list minutes\\\\\\\\n /admin/reports                Upload + list fin. reports\\\\\\\\n /admin/bylaws                 Rich-text edit bylaws\\\\\\\\n /admin/schools                Rich-text edit schools\\\\\\\\n /login                        Firebase/Auth page\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPublic-site pages consume same Firestore data via ISR (see §6).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n2. Editor Choice & Integration Steps\\\\\\\\nChosen component: Tiptap v2 + @tiptap/extension-markdown.\\\\\\\\nIntegration steps:\\\\\\\\n2.1  npm i @tiptap/react @tiptap/starter-kit @tiptap/extension-markdown react-use\\\\\\\\n2.2  Create components/editor/RichTextEditor.tsx – wrapper exposing value/onChange.\\\\\\\\n2.3  Store Markdown in Firestore; render HTML on public pages using marked.\\\\\\\\n2.4  Dynamic import with ssr:false to avoid hydration mismatch.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n3. Firestore Schemas & Storage Layout\\\\\\\\n3.1 Collection news { title, slug, excerpt, bodyMd, coverImageUrl, publishDate, authorUid, isPublished, createdAt, updatedAt }\\\\\\\\n3.2 Collection minutes { title, meetingDate, fileUrl, fileName, uploadedByUid, createdAt }; Storage: minutes/{docId}/{originalName}\\\\\\\\n3.3 Collection financial_reports { name, fiscalYear, fileUrl, fileType, uploadedByUid, createdAt }; Storage: financial-reports/{fiscalYear}/{docId}.{ext}\\\\\\\\n3.4 Document siteContent/bylaws { bodyMd, updatedAt, updatedByUid }\\\\\\\\n3.5 Document siteContent/schools { bodyMd, updatedAt, updatedByUid }\\\\\\\\nSecurity rules: public read for published; write only if role in ['admin','board'].\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n4. Board-Member UI Flow\\\\\\\\n1) /login → Firebase UI.\\\\\\\\n2) On auth success token includes custom claim role.\\\\\\\\n3) middleware.ts protects /admin/*.\\\\\\\\n4) AuthGuard component double-checks client-side.\\\\\\\\n5) DashboardLayout renders Sidebar + child route.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n5. Component/File Inventory\\\\\\\\nmiddleware.ts, firebase/client.ts, firebase/admin.ts, hooks (useAuth, useFirestoreDoc, useUpload), components/editor/RichTextEditor.tsx, UI components (Sidebar, ConfirmDelete), pages under app/admin/* as listed, app/api/revalidate/route.ts, tests/*.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n6. Rendering Strategy\\\\\\\\nPublic pages: ISR (revalidate = 3600) plus manual trigger via /api/revalidate.\\\\\\\\nAdmin pages: CSR inside protected layout; optional RSC list fetch.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n7. Execution-Phase Task Breakdown\\\\\\\\nT1 Auth Middleware & Hooks\\\\\\\\nT2 Tiptap wrapper component\\\\\\\\nT3 News CRUD pages\\\\\\\\nT4 Minutes upload flow + Storage service\\\\\\\\nT5 Financial reports upload flow + Storage service\\\\\\\\nT6 Bylaws & Schools editors\\\\\\\\nT7 Revalidate endpoint + ISR wiring\\\\\\\\nT8 Firestore & Storage security rules\\\\\\\\nT9 Unit tests & lint config\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n8. Deterministic Installation Commands\\\\\\\\nnpm i firebase @firebase/auth @firebase/firestore @firebase/storage\\\\\\\\nnpm i @tiptap/react @tiptap/starter-kit @tiptap/extension-markdown marked\\\\\\\\nnpm i react-use clsx\\\\\\\\nnpm i -D jest @testing-library/react eslint prettier\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n9. Completion Criteria\\\\\\\\n✓ Files compile (tsc).\\\\\\\\n✓ Admin can CRUD News, upload PDFs, edit rich-text pages.\\\\\\\\n✓ Public ISR pages update within 1 h or on manual revalidate.\\\\\\\\n✓ Security rules tested; unauthorized writes rejected.\\\\\\\\n✓ Lighthouse > 90 on public pages.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nEnd of DEP\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-28T00:41:21.895Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###ord_f2###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Great work on the Frontend DEP. However, the Auth and Admin plans both standardize on the Next.js App Router (app/ directory) while your current sitemap is expressed with the legacy pages/ router. Please update your DEP to align with App Router conventions so the three domain plans are consistent. \\\\n\\\\nSpecifically:\\\\n1. Convert every route to the app/ directory format (e.g., app/(public)/bylaws/page.tsx, app/(member)/dues/page.tsx, app/(admin)/dashboard/page.tsx, etc.). \\\\n2. Note layout.tsx files and nested layouts as appropriate (public, member-only, admin).  \\\\n3. Update your ProtectedRoute/AdminRoute strategy to rely on the project-wide middleware.ts written by the Auth team plus a client-side fallback hook (if needed).  \\\\n4. Provide any adjusted file list and delegation map impacted by this router change.  \\\\n\\\\nPlease keep the rest of your DEP intact and resubmit the amended version.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 4,\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"plan-frontend-v2\\\"\\n}\\n###ord_f2###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-28T00:41:51.209Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"ord_f2\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order plan-frontend-v2 from agent 4: **HOA Website – Frontend & UI/UX DEP (App Router-Aligned)**\\\\\\\\nResponsible: Director L\\\\\\\\nPhase: PLANNING (ready for execution)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe DEP below amends v1 to fully adopt the Next.js 13/14 App Router, preserving all prior content where unaffected.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nA. Sitemap & App Router Structure\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nNotation\\\\\\\\n • app/ is implicit root.  \\\\\\\\n • Segments grouped with parentheses () for parallel routing; folders without parentheses are standard.  \\\\\\\\n • Every leaf page lives in **page.tsx**; shared UI in **layout.tsx**; loading & error states optional.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. Public (no auth)\\\\\\\\n  app/(public)/layout.tsx              – PublicLayout (header/footer)\\\\\\\\n  app/(public)/page.tsx                – Home (/)\\\\\\\\n  app/(public)/contact/page.tsx        – /contact\\\\\\\\n  app/(public)/bylaws/page.tsx         – /bylaws\\\\\\\\n  app/(public)/schools/page.tsx        – /schools\\\\\\\\n  app/(public)/login/page.tsx          – /login\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. Member-Only (requires user)\\\\\\\\n  app/(member)/layout.tsx              – MemberLayout (inherits header, adds member nav)\\\\\\\\n  app/(member)/dues/page.tsx           – /dues\\\\\\\\n  app/(member)/meetings/page.tsx       – /meetings\\\\\\\\n  app/(member)/meetings/[year]/page.tsx– /meetings/[year]\\\\\\\\n  app/(member)/news-events/page.tsx    – /news-events\\\\\\\\n  app/(member)/news-events/[slug]/page.tsx – /news-events/[slug]\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. Admin-Only\\\\\\\\n  app/(admin)/layout.tsx               – AdminLayout (sidebar)\\\\\\\\n  app/(admin)/dashboard/page.tsx       – /admin/dashboard\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4. Misc\\\\\\\\n  app/not-found.tsx                    – Custom 404\\\\\\\\n  middleware.ts                        – Auth/role guard (see C-1)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nB. Folder / File List (one per line)\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\napp/\\\\\\\\n  layout.tsx                           // Root – injects ThemeProvider/AuthProvider\\\\\\\\n  globals.css                          // imported in root layout\\\\\\\\n  (public)/layout.tsx\\\\\\\\n  (public)/page.tsx\\\\\\\\n  (public)/contact/page.tsx\\\\\\\\n  (public)/bylaws/page.tsx\\\\\\\\n  (public)/schools/page.tsx\\\\\\\\n  (public)/login/page.tsx\\\\\\\\n  (member)/layout.tsx\\\\\\\\n  (member)/dues/page.tsx\\\\\\\\n  (member)/meetings/page.tsx\\\\\\\\n  (member)/meetings/[year]/page.tsx\\\\\\\\n  (member)/news-events/page.tsx\\\\\\\\n  (member)/news-events/[slug]/page.tsx\\\\\\\\n  (admin)/layout.tsx\\\\\\\\n  (admin)/dashboard/page.tsx\\\\\\\\n  not-found.tsx\\\\\\\\nmiddleware.ts\\\\\\\\ncomponents/\\\\\\\\n  layout/Header.tsx\\\\\\\\n  layout/Footer.tsx\\\\\\\\n  layout/MobileMenu.tsx\\\\\\\\n  ui/Button.tsx\\\\\\\\n  ui/Card.tsx\\\\\\\\n  ui/Modal.tsx\\\\\\\\n  ui/Spinner.tsx\\\\\\\\n  forms/LoginForm.tsx\\\\\\\\ncontext/AuthContext.tsx\\\\\\\\ncontext/ThemeContext.tsx\\\\\\\\nhooks/useAuth.ts\\\\\\\\nhooks/useBreakpoint.ts\\\\\\\\nlib/auth.ts\\\\\\\\nlib/api.ts\\\\\\\\ntailwind.config.js\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nC. Auth & Role Protection Strategy\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nC-1 middleware.ts (shared with Auth domain)\\\\\\\\n • Runs on every request (edge).  \\\\\\\\n • Parses cookies/JWT; determines role.\\\\\\\\n • Redirect matrix:\\\\\\\\n    – Un-authed hitting /(member) or /(admin) → /login?redirect=…  \\\\\\\\n    – Authed non-admin hitting /(admin) → /  \\\\\\\\n • Matcher: `[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"/(member)(.*)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"/(admin)(.*)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]` (plus GET only).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nC-2 Client-side fallback\\\\\\\\n • useAuth() hooks inside member & admin layouts to show a Spinner while validating `user` from context; rare race condition only on CSR navigations.\\\\\\\\n • If `user == null` after hydration, push(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"/login\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\").\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nC-3 Removed: components/layout/ProtectedRoute.tsx & AdminRoute.tsx (redundant).  Kept as **optional** fallback utilities if team decides; but not required.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nD. Layout Nesting Overview\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nRoot layout.tsx\\\\\\\\n  ↳ ThemeProvider / AuthProvider / <html> boilerplate\\\\\\\\n      ↳ (public)/layout.tsx  – public header/footer\\\\\\\\n         ↳ page.tsx etc.\\\\\\\\n      ↳ (member)/layout.tsx  – extends public header, adds member nav tabs\\\\\\\\n         ↳ page.tsx & nested dynamic routes\\\\\\\\n      ↳ (admin)/layout.tsx   – admin sidebar, no public header\\\\\\\\n         ↳ dashboard/page.tsx\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nE. Navigation & Responsiveness (unchanged)\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nHeader/Menu code stays; now imported by (public) & (member) layouts; Admin layout uses its own sidebar.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nF. Style System, Accessibility, etc. (unchanged)\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nNo changes required.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nG. Delegation Map – Revised Paths\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nS-1 Layout & Navigation\\\\\\\\n  • root layout.tsx, (public)/layout.tsx, (member)/layout.tsx, (admin)/layout.tsx\\\\\\\\n  • Header, Footer, MobileMenu components\\\\\\\\nS-2 Public Pages (App Router files)\\\\\\\\n  • (public)/page.tsx, contact/page.tsx, bylaws/page.tsx, schools/page.tsx, login/page.tsx, not-found.tsx\\\\\\\\nS-3 Member Pages\\\\\\\\n  • (member)/dues/page.tsx\\\\\\\\n  • (member)/meetings/page.tsx & [year]/page.tsx\\\\\\\\n  • (member)/news-events/page.tsx & [slug]/page.tsx\\\\\\\\nS-4 Admin Dashboard\\\\\\\\n  • (admin)/dashboard/page.tsx + sidebar & admin widgets\\\\\\\\nS-5 Styling & Theming\\\\\\\\n  • Tailwind setup (globals.css, config)\\\\\\\\nS-6 Middleware & Auth Helpers\\\\\\\\n  • middleware.ts, lib/auth.ts, hooks/useAuth.ts (CSR fallback), tests\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nEach supervisor remains OFAAT-compliant; only their file paths changed.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nNo further external dependencies added; DEP remains deterministic.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-28T00:41:51.209Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###phase1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: PHASE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"All three Director-level DEPs (Frontend/UI, Authentication/Security, and Content-Management/Admin) have been delivered, cross-checked, and reconciled to the same Next.js App-Router architecture.  They are each deterministic, file-level clear, and mutually consistent.  No further open questions remain.  We can therefore compile them into a single, step-ordered Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) for the entire HOA website and proceed to the Execution phase.\\\",\\n  \\\"depString\\\": \\\"────────────────────────────────────────\\\\nHOA WEBSITE – MASTER DETERMINISTICALLY EXECUTABLE PLAN (DEP)\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\nThis document merges the three domain DEPs (Frontend v2, Auth v1, Admin v1) into one execution roadmap.  File paths are relative to repository root.\\\\n\\\\n0. PREREQUISITES\\\\n   • Node 18+  • npm 9+  • Git  • Vercel CLI  • Firebase CLI  • jq (for scripts)\\\\n   • Two Firebase projects already reserved: hoa-portal-dev, hoa-portal-prod.\\\\n   • Vercel account with GitHub linkage.\\\\n\\\\n1. INITIAL REPOSITORY & TOOLING\\\\n   1.1  npx create-next-app@latest hoa-portal --typescript --tailwind --eslint --app --no-src-dir --import-alias \\\\\\\"@/*\\\\\\\"\\\\n   1.2  cd hoa-portal && git init && git remote add origin <repo-url>\\\\n   1.3  npm i firebase @firebase/auth @firebase/firestore @firebase/storage\\\\n   1.4  npm i @tiptap/react @tiptap/starter-kit @tiptap/extension-markdown marked react-use clsx\\\\n   1.5  npm i -D jest @testing-library/react axe-playwright @playwright/test\\\\n\\\\n2. GLOBAL STRUCTURE (App Router)\\\\n   app/\\\\n     layout.tsx              // Root providers\\\\n     globals.css             // Tailwind base\\\\n     (public)/…              // see §2.1\\\\n     (member)/…              // see §2.2\\\\n     (admin)/…               // see §2.3\\\\n     not-found.tsx\\\\n   middleware.ts             // Edge auth/role gate (§3)\\\\n   components/, context/, hooks/, lib/, types/, tailwind.config.js\\\\n\\\\n   2.1 PUBLIC SEGMENT FILES (one file each)\\\\n       (public)/layout.tsx, page.tsx, contact/page.tsx, bylaws/page.tsx,\\\\n       schools/page.tsx, login/page.tsx\\\\n   2.2 MEMBER SEGMENT FILES\\\\n       (member)/layout.tsx, dues/page.tsx, meetings/page.tsx,\\\\n       meetings/[year]/page.tsx, news-events/page.tsx,\\\\n       news-events/[slug]/page.tsx\\\\n   2.3 ADMIN SEGMENT FILES\\\\n       (admin)/layout.tsx, dashboard/page.tsx (+ sidebar components)\\\\n\\\\n3. AUTHENTICATION & SECURITY IMPLEMENTATION\\\\n   3.1  firebase.json, .firebaserc → alias dev/prod projectIds.\\\\n   3.2  src/lib/firebaseClient.ts – initialise SDK with env vars.\\\\n   3.3  src/lib/firebaseAdmin.ts  – Admin SDK w/ credential cache.\\\\n   3.4  context/AuthContext.tsx & hooks/useAuth.ts – client auth state.\\\\n   3.5  middleware.ts – edge JWT verification; matcher:[\\\\\\\"/(member)(.*)\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"/(admin)(.*)\\\\\\\"]\\\\n   3.6  functions/ (using Firebase Functions v2)\\\\n        • auth/onCreate.ts – default resident role claim.\\\\n        • https/setRole.ts – callable only by admin.\\\\n   3.7  firestore.rules & storage.rules – copy from Auth DEP §E, F.\\\\n   3.8  scripts/set-remote-config.ts – toggle socialAuthEnabled param.\\\\n\\\\n4. CONTENT-MANAGEMENT / ADMIN DASHBOARD\\\\n   4.1  components/editor/RichTextEditor.tsx – Tiptap wrapper.\\\\n   4.2  hooks/useFirestoreDoc.ts, useUpload.ts – CRUD helpers.\\\\n   4.3  app/(admin)/news/* pages – list, new, [id].\\\\n        app/(admin)/minutes/*, financial reports, bylaws, schools editors.\\\\n   4.4  Storage upload paths: minutes/{docId}/{file}, financial-reports/{year}/{docId}.{ext}\\\\n   4.5  app/api/revalidate/route.ts – triggers ISR for affected paths.\\\\n\\\\n5. FRONTEND UI & THEMING\\\\n   5.1  components/layout/Header.tsx, Footer.tsx, MobileMenu.tsx\\\\n   5.2  Tailwind theme extension in tailwind.config.js (brand colours etc.).\\\\n   5.3  Responsive nav logic (useBreakpoint).  Mobile ≤768px hamburger.\\\\n   5.4  Accessibility: add skip-link, focus outlines, contrast tests (axe).\\\\n\\\\n6. ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES\\\\n   .env.local.sample containing:\\\\n     NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=\\\\n     NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=\\\\n     NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=\\\\n     NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=\\\\n     NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=\\\\n     NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=\\\\n     NEXT_PUBLIC_REMOTE_CONFIG_DEFAULTS='{\\\\\\\"socialAuthEnabled\\\\\\\":false}'\\\\n     COOKIE_SECRET_SIGNING=\\\\n     FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY_JSON=\\\\n   • Add same (encrypted) in Vercel for dev & prod.\\\\n\\\\n7. QUALITY & TESTS\\\\n   • ESLint/Prettier pre-commit via Husky.\\\\n   • jest + @testing-library for unit tests of components.\\\\n   • Playwright a11y test running axe-core on key pages.\\\\n   • GitHub Actions CI: lint, type-check, test, build.\\\\n\\\\n8. DEPLOYMENT PIPELINE\\\\n   8.1  vercel link –project \\\\\\\"hoa-portal\\\\\\\" –yes\\\\n   8.2  vercel env pull .env.local\\\\n   8.3  git push origin main → triggers Vercel build & preview URL.\\\\n   8.4  On merge to main, Vercel promotes to Production.\\\\n   8.5  firebase deploy --only firestore:rules,storage:rules,functions --project hoa-portal-prod (run from CI).\\\\n\\\\n9. EXECUTION-PHASE WORK PACKAGE LIST (OFAAT)\\\\n   Supervisor-Frontend\\\\n     • S1 Layout & Navigation (root, public, member, admin layouts + Header/Footer)\\\\n     • S2 Public Pages\\\\n     • S3 Member Pages\\\\n   Supervisor-AdminCMS\\\\n     • S4 Admin Dashboard pages + RichTextEditor + upload services\\\\n     • S5 ISR & revalidate API route\\\\n   Supervisor-AuthSec\\\\n     • S6 middleware.ts, Auth context/hook, firebase client/admin libs\\\\n     • S7 Firestore & Storage rules, Cloud Functions, remote-config script\\\\n   Supervisor-Infra\\\\n     • S8 Firebase project CLI setup, env vars, GitHub/Vercel secrets\\\\n     • S9 CI pipeline YAML, lint/test workflows\\\\n   Supervisor-QA/Accessibility\\\\n     • S10 Unit tests, axe Playwright suite\\\\n\\\\n10. COMPLETION CRITERIA (Definition of Done)\\\\n   ✓ Build passes locally & in CI (tsc, eslint, jest).\\\\n   ✓ Visiting /dues unauth redirects to /login.\\\\n   ✓ Resident can view /news-events; boardMember can access /admin/*.\\\\n   ✓ Admin can create News item; public page shows within ≤1 h or on revalidate.\\\\n   ✓ Firebase rules dry-run passes with zero violations.\\\\n   ✓ Lighthouse score ≥90 and axe-core reports zero critical issues.\\\\n   ✓ Production deployed on Vercel and domain mapped.\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\nEND OF MASTER DEP\\\"\\n}\\n###phase1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-28T00:43:00.099Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"phase1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"DENIED_BY_INTERNAL_REVIEW\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Phase shift was denied by internal review. Feedback from Partagaz D:\\\\\\\\nDENY\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe DEP is well-structured but omits two explicit user requirements, so it cannot be approved as-is:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. No member-accessible route or UI is defined for viewing “financial reports” (the user specifically asked that residents be able to view these after login). Only an admin-side uploader path is mentioned.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. The Contact Us page is listed, but there is no deterministic implementation of the “contact form” (submission endpoint, email/Firestore storage, spam protection, etc.). Merely having /contact/page.tsx is insufficient.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nUntil a protected Financial Reports member page (with its route, data fetch logic, and Firestore paths) and a fully-specified contact form (frontend fields plus backend handler) are added, the plan does not fully satisfy the stated goals.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-28T00:43:00.099Z###\"}]}],\"config\":{},\"tools\":[],\"output\":{}}}","genkit:state":"success"},"displayName":"generate","links":[],"instrumentationLibrary":{"name":"genkit-tracer","version":"v1"},"spanKind":"INTERNAL","sameProcessAsParentSpan":{"value":true},"status":{"code":0},"timeEvents":{"timeEvent":[]}}},"displayName":"generate","startTime":1753663380148,"endTi